# No shell commands

The agent shell is unusable here. The repo lives in WSL (`/home/qlebastard/qmk_userspace_bstiq`)
while the shell host is Windows PowerShell, so POSIX commands are mangled, `wsl bash -lc "..."`
wrappers return no exit status, and long commands like `qmk compile` kill the session.

Do not call the shell tool. That includes `git`, `qmk`, `make`, `ls`, `cat`, and anything wrapped
in `wsl`.

## Instead

- Use the file tools (read, search, glob, edit) for everything the shell would have been used for.
- Verify changes by reading the code back and checking the linter. Count fixed-width sprite rows
  and array bounds by hand.
- Never claim a build passed. Say what was verified and what was not, then give the user the exact
  command to run.

```
# ❌ BAD
wsl bash -lc "cd ~/qmk_userspace_bstiq && qmk compile -kb bastardkb/dilemma/4x6_4_procyon -km vendor"

# ✅ GOOD — in the reply, for the user to run in their own WSL terminal
qmk compile -c -kb bastardkb/dilemma/4x6_4_procyon -km vendor
```

## Git

No `git` calls either: no `status`, `diff`, `add`, `commit`, or `push`. Describe the edits made and
let the user commit. `compile_all_keymaps.sh` is likewise theirs to run.
